   "he": "וּפוֹטֵר מִן הַיִּבּוּם. ״וּבֵן אֵין לוֹ״ אָמַר רַחֲמָנָא, וְהָא אִית לֵיהּ.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «And» a one-day-old baby «exempts» his widowed mother «from the» obligation of «levirate marriage.» The Gemara explains the derivation: «The Merciful One states:» “And one of them dies, «and he has no child”» (Deuteronomy 25:5), «and this» late husband «has» a child, albeit one who is one day old."
  }
